Nested (no-steam) gamescope: hide the overlay by unmapping, not opacity

Opening and closing the hhd overlay inside a nested gamescope session left
the game on a permanent black screen: the old code hid the window with
_NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY=0 and tagged it STEAM_GAME/STEAM_BIGPICTURE, which
makes gamescope key its app/scene handling off the window and desync it
from the real game (DXVK present loop then starves and the game stops
rendering while all X-side focus state looks healthy).

Nested sessions have no WM, so the overlay window is now simply mapped on
top while shown and unmapped while hidden:

- prepare_hhd: do not tag STEAM_GAME/STEAM_BIGPICTURE or touch opacity;
  unmap Electron's initially-mapped window right away (it used to be
  hidden by opacity=0) and select StructureNotify so a later Electron
  re-show wakes the overlay loop.
- show_hhd/hide_hhd: nested branch maps/unmaps only; STEAM_INPUT_FOCUS /
  STEAM_OVERLAY writes are done only when a Steam client exists.
- loop_manage_overlay: re-unmap every tick while the UI is closed so
  Electron can never leave its black window covering the game.

Verified on the Legion Go nested sessions (Skyrim SE via Proton): game
renders from boot, QAM open/close no longer blackscreens it.

